             pphhyyssiioo().

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     If successful pphhyyssiioo() returns 0.  EFAULT is returned if the address
     range described by _u_i_o is not accessible by the requesting process.
     pphhyyssiioo() will return any error resulting from calls to the device strat‐
     egy routine, by examining the B_ERROR buffer flag and the _b___e_r_r_o_r field.
     Note that the actual transfer size may be less than requested by _u_i_o if
     the device signals an “end of file” condition.

